@startuml catch_up_chip_states
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' catch_up_chip_states — v26.7 (catch-up §K.5).
'
' The point of the picture: every transition into MUTED is reversible from
' TWO directions — the user's tap (transient, snooze survives) or the
' evening reset (automatic, snooze lapses) — and NO state locks the drawer.
' Access and attention are separate axes; only attention has states.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

title The catch-up chip — three intensities, one always-open door

state "ABSENT\n(card hidden)" as absent
state "PROMINENT\namber · «N to catch up»" as prom
state "MUTED\ngray · «N · back 22:30»" as muted

[*] --> absent

absent --> prom : a block ends short\n(at a moment, not snoozed)
absent --> muted : resolved blocks exist\n(«N resolved» — the way back)

prom --> muted : «Later»\n(snooze until the reset)
prom --> muted : moment toggle off\n(Settings → Catch-up)
muted --> prom : the reset\n(evening moment / snooze lapses)

prom --> absent : last block resolved\nand recovery window empty
muted --> absent : horizon ages the\nlast block out (§C)

note right of muted
  Clicking the MUTED chip opens the
  drawer but does NOT clear the snooze:
  the midday review is transient —
  prominence returns only at the reset.
  (Owner's workflow: quiet workday,
  deliberate re-summon, guaranteed
  evening return.)
end note

note bottom of prom
  The drawer is reachable from every
  visible state. It holds ALL verbs:
  Move → , Done, Skip, Skip all,
  the undo receipt, bring-back, Later.
  The glance panel reads; the drawer does.
end note

@enduml
